      "writtenOn": "2026-07-13T16:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something to consider. Our ID Header VDO is pretty consistent. IIUC the PDCs default ID Header is usually correct. We only need to update it when the device is also a UFP.\n\nShould we instead gate this init state on `usb_comm_capable_as_device` so it just gets skipped for most devices? It would lead to fewer commands to the PDC on init.",
      "revId": "fb0499c712a90c0dbc6e3e1f51b70f7e558669b2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23780888_3e5a041e",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 1758,
      "author": {
        "id": 3773521
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-14T08:28:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, on the other hand I don\u0027t want to branch out during the init. I think current solution is easier to follow and gives control over it for the future. Also in the next CL I am adding setting DFP and UFP, for DFP it is always present but we will be able to modify specific attributes for it, what makes it more consistent.",
      "parentUuid": "f100ec03_001e3229",
      "revId": "fb0499c712a90c0dbc6e3e1f51b70f7e558669b2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
